  D. The newer ones had more character
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q3: What makes the new ballparks intimate?
  A. The size of the land on which they are built
  B. Wood construction
  C. Architectural design
  D. Better amenities
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q4: Which is true?
  A. All newer ballparks have top-level seating closer to the field than ever
  B. Newer ballparks do not have upper deck seating
  C. All newer ballparks have top-level seating further away from the field than ever
  D. Some newer ballparks have top-level seating further away from the field than ever
  Gold answer: D (4)

Q5: Choose the one best statement.
  A. A majority of teams either built new ballparks in the last decade or plan to build soon
  B. Almost no teams either built new ballparks in the last decade or plan to build soon
  C. All teams either built new ballparks in the last decade or plan to build soon
  D. Some teams either built new ballparks in the last decade or plan to build soon
  Gold answer: A (1)

Q6: Which is not true?
  A. Some ballparks are subsidized by taxpayers
  B. People get more affordable tickets because the ballpark is subsidized
  C. Some ballparks are built in urban locations
  D. Some team owners pay to build their own ballparks
  Gold answer: B (2)

Q7: What is something new parks have that old parks did not?
