  A. The pilot of Flight 26
  B. Russians
  C. Two boys
  D. Mt. Palomar
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q11: Why did Solomon send cars into space?
  A. He wanted room
  B. He did it on accident
  C. He was bored
  D. He thought it would be fun
  Gold answer: A (1)

Q12: What is the tone of this story?
  A. Humorous
  B. Serious
  C. Dramatic
  D. Suspenseful
  Gold answer: A (1)

Q13: Why did the Russians want to send cars into space?
  A. They didn't want to
  B. They have strategic value
  C. To get revenge on the Americans
  D. To compete with the Americans
  Gold answer: D (4)

Q14: How do Solomon's flying cars work?
  A. We never learn
  B. Combustion
  C. Pressure
  D. Hubcaps
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q15: Why didn't Solomon destroy the old cars instead?
  A. He liked them too much
  B. He didn't have the means
  C. They were worth too much
  D. He was not allowed
  Gold answer: A (1)

Q16: What did the matches help Solomon with?
