  C. Hoshick decided it would be better for the Flapjacks to return to Jax, and this put an end to the conflict.
  D. It turns out that the Flapjacks wanted land that the colonists considered worthless, so it was easy to reach an agreement in priniciple.
  Gold answer: D (4)
