  A. They went on to challenge the squid
  B. There was no change
  C. They developed space travel
  D. They took over the planet
  Gold answer: B (2)

Q10: Of the following options, which best summarizes this story?
  A. Men study a planet to see where they should colonize and learn the natural resources potential of the planet.
  B. Men study the interspecies interactions on a planet to learn whether they're allowed to colonize the planet.
  C. Men study the interspecies interactions on a planet to make sense of them to learn whether the planet is safe to inhabit.
  D. Men study a planet to see where they should colonize and learn more about the strange customs of the fishermen.
  Gold answer: B (2)

Q11: Of the following options, which traits best describe Arthur Farrell?
  A. witty and considerate
  B. smart and reckless
  C. stubborn and talkative
  D. calculated and cautious
  Gold answer: B (2)

Q12: Of the following options, which technology is not used in the story?
  A. Radio-like communication
  B. A chemical that prevents a person from moving
  C. Ships that can submerge to examine deep waters
  D. Tablets used to enhance rest
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q13: Did the characters accomplish their goal?
  A. No. The characters had many questions, some of which were resolved, but a few important ones were left unanswered.
  B. No. The characters learned something they didn't want to know and it caused them to want to defy orders.
  C. Yes. They learned what they wanted to learn and made good choices based on what they learned.
  D. Yes. Not only did they learn what they needed to, but they had fun interactions with the species on the planet which improved their understanding.
  Gold answer: C (3)

Q14: What is the narrative purpose of having Arthur try to explore Arz while Stryker slept?
  A. It was to increase the reader's curiosity because Arthur didn't know what the inside of the island looked like.
  B. It was to help the reader learn answers to the questions they had.
  C. It was to allow Arthur to communicate with the fishermen and learn more about their customs.
  D. It was to build suspense because Arthur was put in harm's way.
  Gold answer: D (4)

Q15: Based on the reading, of the three main characters who should you want to go on an expedition with the least, and why?
  A. Gibson. He's so independent that he's not one for teamwork and it teamwork makes adventures more fun.
